  "comments": [
    {
      "paragraph_index": 5,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "comment": "Prepare all solutions and autoclave under a N2 atmosphere. After cooling,combine the solutions and replace the gas phase with a N2--CO2 (4:1, v/v) gas mixture. Then, aseptically and anaerobically add the following autoclaved or *filter--sterilized solutions to the medium:"
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 8,
      "comment": "Check the final pH of the medium to be around 7.3."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 9,
      "comment": "Comment: JCM 14587 grows also in a modified medium with benzene and chlorate. For preparation of the modified medium, replace NaNO3 with 1.06 g NaClO3 (in 900 ml solution A). After combining all solutions (A, B and C), add 1.0 ml/L of 1.0 M sodium acetate solution (autoclaved), 25 ml/L of 20 mM benzene (water-saturated, autoclaved), and 1 ml/L of each of vitamin solution (see Medium No. [403], filter-sterilized), thiamine solution (see Medium No. [403], filter-sterilized) and vitamin B12 solution (see Medium No. [403], filter-sterilized) to the medium. Otherwise, prepare the modified medium as described above."
    }
  ]
}